---
// The in-game addon's page: what it does, where to download it (config.addonUrls), how to install and start.
// Linked from the header's "Get the addon" button and the home page hero.
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import PageHero from "../components/PageHero.astro";
import config from "../config.js";
import Icon from "../components/Icon.astro";

const links = [
  config.addonUrls?.curseforge && { href: config.addonUrls.curseforge, label: "CurseForge", note: "the most used addon app and site" },
  config.addonUrls?.wago && { href: config.addonUrls.wago, label: "Wago", note: "Wago Addons and the Wago app" },
].filter(Boolean) as { href: string; label: string; note: string }[];
---
<BaseLayout
  title="Forever Anvil addon for WoW: Forever | Auction prices in game"
  description="Free WoW: Forever addon: auction prices, sales per day and disenchant value on every tooltip, flips and upgrades tagged in the auction house, craft profits and a leveling helper in your profession window."
  page="addon"
>
  <PageHero icon="prices" eyebrow="In-game addon" title="Forever Anvil in your game" facts={[{ icon: "clock", text: "Fresh prices several times a day" }, { icon: "check", text: "Free, no account" }, { icon: "globe", text: "Europe and the Americas" }]}>
    The same auction prices as this site, right where you need them: on every item tooltip, in the auction house and in your profession window.
    <div class="hero-actions" slot="actions">
      {links.map((l, i) => <a class:list={["btn", { "btn-ghost": i > 0 }]} href={l.href} target="_blank" rel="noopener"><Icon name="download" size={20} />Download on {l.label}</a>)}
      {config.discordUrl && <a class="btn btn-ghost" href={config.discordUrl} target="_blank" rel="noopener"><Icon name="discord" size={20} />Help &amp; ideas on Discord</a>}
    </div>
  </PageHero>

  <div class="wrap section grid grid-2">
    <div class="panel">
      <h2>What it shows</h2>
      <h3>Item tooltips</h3>
      <p>For the auction house you're on (your ruleset and faction, or the neutral Blackwater house when you're at one):</p>
      <ul class="gems">
        <li><b>Market price</b> and <b>lowest listed price</b>, with how many are listed</li>
        <li><b>Sold per day</b>, estimated from how listings change hour to hour</li>
        <li><b>Region median</b>: the typical price across the region's auction houses</li>
        <li><b>Disenchant value</b> after the auction cut, and the Enchanting skill it needs</li>
        <li><b>Upgrades</b>: gear with a higher item level than what you wear in that slot, that your class can use at your level</li>
        <li><b>Waylaid crates</b>: the Merchant's Favor a crate pays and the cheapest bundle to fill it</li>
      </ul>
      <h3>Auction house</h3>
      <ul class="gems">
        <li><b>Disenchant flips</b>: gear listed for less than its enchanting materials sell for, tagged <code>DE +X</code> in the Browse list</li>
        <li><b>Vendor flips</b>: items listed for less than a vendor pays, tagged <code>Vendor +X</code></li>
        <li><b>Your watchlist</b>: items at or below your target price, tagged <code>Target</code></li>
        <li><b>Your shopping list</b>: materials you still need, tagged <code>Need X</code>, and a small list beside the auction house that ticks off what's in your bags and bank</li>
        <li><b>Upgrades</b> for your character, tagged <code>Upgrade +X</code></li>
        <li><b>Scan</b>: the button under the auction house window (or <b>/fa scan</b> there) reads every auction and uses those prices right away, so you have current prices between addon updates (one scan every 15 minutes)</li>
        <li>Optional: every disenchantable item's value in grey, to see how close it is to a flip</li>
      </ul>
      <h3>Profession window</h3>
      <ul class="gems">
        <li><b>Profit per craft</b> on every recipe, after the 5% auction cut and the reagents</li>
        <li><b>Leveling helper</b>: the recipe you know that gives skill points for the least gold right now is marked <code>skill-up</code>, with its chance and cost per point</li>
        <li>The selected recipe's reagent cost; reagents that aren't on the auction house use the vendor's price</li>
      </ul>
      <h3>Prices window</h3>
      <ul class="gems">
        <li><b>Every item on your auction house</b>, like this site's <a href="/prices">prices page</a>: search by name, pick a category, sort by market, lowest price, units listed or sold per day (<b>/fa prices</b>, or the minimap menu)</li>
        <li>Switch to the other faction's house or the neutral one, and click an item for its details, to watch it or to add it to your shopping list</li>
      </ul>
      <h3>Upgrades for you</h3>
      <ul class="gems">
        <li>Like this site's <a href="/upgrades">upgrade finder</a>, for the character you're playing, and ranked for your talent spec: gear on sale that's better for you than what you wear, with gear made for other specs left out, within your budget (<b>/fa upgrades</b>, or the minimap menu)</li>
      </ul>
      <h3>Bag value</h3>
      <ul class="gems">
        <li>What everything in your bags is worth, and the best way to sell each item: the auction house, disenchanting or a vendor (<b>/fa bags</b>, or the minimap menu)</li>
        <li><b>Right-click</b> an item you're keeping to leave it out of the total</li>
      </ul>
      <h3>Your watchlist and shopping list</h3>
      <ul class="gems">
        <li><b>Alt-click</b> any item to watch it, and set a target price in the watchlist window (<b>/fa watch</b>)</li>
        <li>In a profession window, the bag button beside <b>Create All</b> adds a recipe's reagents for as many crafts as the quantity box says (<b>/fa list</b> shows the list)</li>
        <li>Both windows show each item's icon, with buttons to edit or remove it, and an editor to add more. Or bring your lists from this site: press <b>Copy for the addon</b> on your <a href="/watchlist">watchlist</a> or <a href="/planner">crafting planner</a>, then type <b>/fa import</b> in game and paste it.</li>
      </ul>
    </div>

    <div class="panel">
      <h2>Download</h2>
      {links.length ? (
        <ul class="addon-dl">
          {links.map((l) => (
            <li>
              <a class="btn" href={l.href} target="_blank" rel="noopener"><Icon name="download" size={20} />Download on {l.label}</a>
              <span class="faint">{l.note}</span>
            </li>
          ))}
        </ul>
      ) : <p>Download links are coming soon.</p>}
      <p>A new version with the latest prices comes out once a day; turn on auto-update in your addon app to always have it. For current prices in between, press Scan at the auction house (or type <code>/fa scan</code> there): the addon reads every auction and uses those prices right away. It tells you in chat when your prices are over two days old, or when someone in your guild or group has newer ones.</p>

      <h2>Getting started</h2>
      <ol>
        <li>Install it with the {links.map((l) => l.label).join(" or ") || "CurseForge or Wago"} app, picking <b>WoW: Forever</b> as the game version. Or download the zip and unpack all its folders (<code>ForeverAnvil</code>, <code>ForeverAnvil_Data_EU</code> and <code>ForeverAnvil_Data_US</code>) into your game's <code>Interface/AddOns</code> folder.</li>
        <li>Log in. The first time, a small window asks which ruleset you play on (PvP, Normal, Roleplay or RP-PvP): one click. Change it later from the minimap menu or with <b>/fa ruleset</b>.</li>
        <li>Click the crest on your minimap for the menu: your lists, quick on/off switches and the settings (also <b>/fa options</b>).</li>
      </ol>

      <h2>Good to know</h2>
      <ul class="gems">
        <li><b>It never buys, sells or crafts for you.</b> It only shows numbers; every action is still your own click.</li>
        <li><b>Prices are an estimate</b> from the last update or your last scan, and the auction house moves. Check before a big purchase.</li>
        <li><b>Europe and the Americas.</b> The addon picks your region by itself and loads only its prices.</li>
        <li><b>English, German, French and Spanish.</b> The addon follows your game client's language.</li>
        <li><b>Upgrades go by item level</b>, which is a shortlist, not a verdict: a strength sword is no upgrade for a healer.</li>
        <li>For price history, full leveling routes and talents, use <a href="/">this site</a>: everything here stays free.</li>
      </ul>
      <p class="faint">Data provided by Blizzard Entertainment. Forever Anvil is a fan project, not made or endorsed by Blizzard.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .addon-dl { list-style: none; padding: 0; margin: 0 0 14px; display: grid; gap: 12px; }
  .addon-dl li { display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 12px; flex-wrap: wrap; }
  .addon-dl .btn { min-width: 220px; justify-content: center; }
  .panel h3 { margin-top: 1.1em; }
</style>
